    "enable": "Modbus TCP runs on the Ethernet port; RS-485 address, baud rate and stop bits/parity are parameters 0, 1 and 3 (front buttons or Modbus).",
    "watchdog": null,
    "quirks": [
      "Addresses are used as printed (0-based).",
      "Floats are ABCD; add 32768 to an address for little-endian.",
      "Energy is in Wh and varh, not kWh.",
      "Rotation field (19052) is a float: 1, 0 or -1."
    ],
    "setup": [
      "RS-485 defaults: address 1, 115.2 kbps.",
      "Set CT/VT ratios (parameters 10-32) so the float values read in primary units.",
      "Writing 1 to 507 clears all energy counters; 506 clears min/max values."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "The RS-485 default is 115.2 kbps (parameter 1 = 4); set the master to match or lower the meter rate.",
      "This list is for the -E model; the basic UMG 96RM uses a different address list."
